\solo plays only the instruments given as arguments and
mutes all others.
Its syntax is the following:

\solo \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. The solo instruments are unmuted, if they
have been muted before.
To play all instruments again, call:

\solo \all

While the sequencer is playing, the change takes effect at
the start of the next bar. If the sequencer is stopped, it
takes effect at once.
To solo instruments immediately, use \solonow.

Muted instruments show a whole rest in the score and are
hidden in the piano roll.

\solo needs at least one argument. An argument that is not
an instrument results in an "unknown instrument" error.
